{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths","id":1092218,"title":"Post your homebrew kiths!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T21:21:55-07:00","id":1092218,"title":"Post your homebrew kiths!","content":"Now that we have guidelines to create our own kiths, it would be nice to see what we can come up with. So if you have an idea for a kith, post it here!<br /> <br /> I'll begin with something inspired by legends from home:<br /> <br /> Ti Sapoti:<br /> Ti Sapoti are a complex kith, charming, playful and mischievous a moment, sinister and frightening the next, they like to keep others guessing, the better to surprise them when the time comes. Originating in Western Africa, Ti Sapoti have become common in the West Indies and the north-west of South America, and some have followed the movement of mortal populations toward North America and Europe to find new playing grounds. Ti Sapoti share a love of novelty, change and surprise, and enjoy sharing that love with others... not always bothering to ask for the others' permission first. A Ti Sapoti's greatest fear is boredom, and they can't conceive of others not sharing the sentiment. Fortunately for them, they have a knack to talk themselves out of trouble, and should it not be enough, they are not as defenseless as they appear to be. Due to their love of misdirection, Ti Sapoti have a hard time forming more than shallow relationships, and will cherish any true friend they have, showering them with gifts and exuberant demonstrations of affection, although those displays tend to be random and sporadic. Likewise those that incur their displeasure can expect some malicious pranks as retribution at the most unexpected moments.<br /> <br /> -Appearance: Ti Sapoti tend to be short, with pleasant, youthful features, large sparkling eyes, round cheeks and agile fingers. These fae always look younger than they actually are, and even when reaching old age they somehow always look adorable. They often appear somewhat disheveled, as if they had dressed in haste or had just been roughhousing. Ti Sapoti range in appearance, but many are of West African ancestry, though often mixed to diverse degrees with one or several others ethnicities, usually Amerindian, European, Indian or East Asian.<br /> More distinctively, their Faerie Miens have backwards facing feet, which surprisingly doesn't seem to hamper them.<br /> <br /> -Lifestyles: Seelie Ti Sapoti are gregarious and love living with as many friends and family as they can, which is a nightmare to anyone liking to keep their home well-ordered. They tend to be a boisterous and inclusive lot, laughing, joking, dancing and singing with abandon, while those around them get caught in their wake. Unseelie Ti Sapoti often prefer to live alone or in smaller groups, are more prone to lead nomadic existences and dedicate themselves to make sure the people around them lead interesting lives while they watch and laugh from the shadows. Both Seelie and Unseelie Ti Sapoti love learning and teaching, especially when it comes to magic and they consider the relationship between professor and student to be sacred. The one thing this kith takes seriously is the sharing of skills and knowlege, though it won't stop them from trying to make a lecture more lively.<br /> <br /> -Childling: Ti Sapoti childlings are adorable and they know it. Insatiably curious, they'll poke their noses everywhere, asking a thousand questions about everything and touching anything they can reach. They tend to congregate around whoever can best satisfy their curiosity and follow them around like ducklings, being polite, attentive and surprisingly obedient, until something or someone else catch their fancy.<br /> <br /> -Wilder: All ti Sapoti like learning, but Wilders do more than just learn. They experiment, often to the consternation of whoever is caught in the blast. Unsatisfied with merely asking questions, they'll try to find their own answers and are either lost in contemplation or throwing themselves into some new activity they hope will be enlightening. They love showing off and inventing new tricks to amaze their friends, or new pranks to surprise them. Nothing is ever good enough as it is for a Ti Sapoti Wilder, including other people's lives, they have to put their own spin on it to be satisfied.<br /> <br /> -Grump: Grumps are done experimenting, they have mastered and refined their skills and are now using them to reach more sophisticated and tangible goals. They almost always take on a few students both to transmit what they know and to have help with their current projects. They play the roles of advisors, diplomats and puppet masters, hiding their true purposes under layers of playfulness and good humor made more effective by the fact thay they're not faked.<br /> <br /> -Affinty: Prop<br /> <br /> -Revelry: Ti Sapoti love startling and destabilizing people, regaining glamour when they do something unexpected, like pulling a prank or offering a surprise gift. They also gain glamour from learning and teaching.<br /> <br /> -Unleashing: Ti Sapoti cantrips are accompanied by the sounds of children's laughing, ominous murmurs, faerie lights and shadows twisting or dancing.<br /> <br /> *Birthrights<br /> -Beautiful Liar: Ti Sapoti gain +1 Appearance and +1 to Manipulation to represent their deceptively cute aspect even if this take them over five.<br /> -Curse of Disorientation: By spending a point of Glamour, a Ti Sapoti can curse someone to become lost and tired. The Ti Sapoti makes an opposed Manipulation + Subterfuge roll resisted by the target's willpower, causing the target to become unable to orient herself and to suffer a wound penalty at the Mauled level for one round per success.<br /> <br /> *Frailty<br /> -Chaos Bringer: Ti Sapoti can't help but leave change and chaos in their wake. Once per scene, they need to change something in a way that people will eventually notice as proof of their passage in an area, which usually means introducing, moving, removing or altering an object. To resist this compulsion the player must make a succesful Willpower roll (difficulty 8).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":".  Edited the Frailty 05-19-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:58:14-07:00","id":1092230,"title":"","content":"Overall pretty neat and evocative, though the frailty could get a bit debilitating as far as getting up to skullduggery of whatever stripe, for any of them inclined to shenanigans like that. Then again they could be the sort of sneak that likes to leave a calling card. The Night Fox and that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T23:08:04-07:00","id":1092248,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I tried to make the Frailty something that would be inconveniencing, thematic and sure to intervene in game without being crippling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:09:11-07:00","id":1092384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1092248#post1092248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I tried to make the Frailty something that would be inconveniencing, thematic and sure to intervene in game without being crippling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get the intent but it might be too crippling as is, for example for me to go to the bathroom from my bedroom I'd have to pass through 3 rooms just in my house. Maybe something like any location they've spent a scene in they have to do the wp thing to leave it without messing with something. that way its not bogged down in crazy inertia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T09:13:22-07:00","id":1092838,"title":"","content":"Would making the compulsion's effect take place in each building rather than each room be better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:31:04-07:00","id":1092911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1092838#post1092838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would making the compulsion's effect take place in each building rather than each room be better?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My thought is anything you've had a legitimate &quot;Scene&quot; in is probably best so they leave calling cards in mansions and probably have to do the wp thing to not be easier to track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T10:58:20-07:00","id":1093338,"title":"","content":"Or just say 'area' instead of 'room'. It's vague enough to not be too hampering, and can be flexible enough for the ST to adjudicate...although I guess that is similar to saying 'scene' but perhaps a little more permissive in the case of, sat, spending the night in a freehold (which could constitute an 'area')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:26:56-07:00","id":1093562,"title":"","content":"This thread tempts me to make a kith or two and I would do so gladly. I immediately thought of Einherjar and Valkyries. <br /> <br /> But intergrating them into already celtocentric universe with all these elaborate kithain backstories is a headache.<br /> <br /> Maybe, I should do as a professional World of Darkness writer and ignore the rest of the canon, if it doesn't mesh with my personal ideas, but I see it as a cop-out. Thoughts, advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-17-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T01:13:15-07:00","id":1093576,"title":"","content":"I can see Valkyries, but how do you plan to do Einherjar? Immortal warrior Souls?<br /> <br /> I was planning on making Einherjar into a sect of Mummies in my game. Yeah go for it, don't worry about contradiction. You don't even need to change much, I mean House Aesin seem to be the Aesir/Vanir Alfar.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of Swan Maidens myself as one of my house kiths, and those would be like a type of Valkyrie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T01:36:26-07:00","id":1093582,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how Einherjar would be different than just a specialized afterlife. Also not sure what Valkyries would do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T10:15:29-07:00","id":1093690,"title":"","content":"In my games, einherjar and valkyries are a number of different things all sharing the same label, but---primarily, these two groups are keremet Adhene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:12:06-07:00","id":1093708,"title":"","content":"I like the keremeth as an idea, but I don't like that they're considered the only way for Enchanted dead and their description/Birthrights/Frailty are oddly specific. Good, but not for everybody.<br /> <br /> Also, Valkyries are not humans nor ever were unlike Einherjar, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:22:15-07:00","id":1093713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1093708#post1093708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the keremeth as an idea, but I don't like that they're considered the only way for Enchanted dead and their description/Birthrights/Frailty are oddly specific. Good, but not for everybody.<br /> <br /> Also, Valkyries are not humans nor ever were unlike Einherjar, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, in my games, keremet are not the <i>only</i> einherjar or valkyries: some are spirits, some are Kami; some are wraiths; and so on. But yes, in <i>my</i> games, 3/5ths of the 'Norse warrior-angel' population <i>is</i> keremet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:30:52-07:00","id":1093866,"title":"","content":"Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T03:42:35-07:00","id":1094481,"title":"","content":"Reminds me I need to do some writeups for Australian Dreamings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T17:53:02-07:00","id":1094730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1093562#post1093562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread tempts me to make a kith or two and I would do so gladly. I immediately thought of Einherjar and Valkyries.<br /> <br /> But intergrating them into already celtocentric universe with all these elaborate kithain backstories is a headache.<br /> <br /> Maybe, I should do as a professional World of Darkness writer and ignore the rest of the canon, if it doesn't mesh with my personal ideas, but I see it as a cop-out. Thoughts, advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Durarara (also spelled DRRR!) had an idea about how to do that, linking Valkyries with Dullahans. Durarara is pretty crazy, though, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T20:35:47-07:00","id":1096583,"title":"","content":"The Kitsune may be Fera but I'm working on a Kith that will be based on the Kumiho/Huli-Jing, I am considering making them Hsien though but I'm trying to figure out how I'd go on about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:17:26-07:00","id":1097453,"title":"","content":"I've been gettig stuck back in to the Nahuali for the Kingdoms of the Featherd Serpent project, but I've hit a snag. I can't figure out what to call their seemings. It doesn't feel right to use the kithain terms, or the Nunnahi, but I can't seem to find anew equivalent in Spanish or Mayan (or any other native language). Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:18:35-07:00","id":1097454,"title":"","content":"(PS. If it's going too far off he initial purpose of the thread I'll shove off to another one :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T02:12:24-07:00","id":1097465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1097453#post1097453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been gettig stuck back in to the Nahuali for the Kingdoms of the Featherd Serpent project, but I've hit a snag. I can't figure out what to call their seemings. It doesn't feel right to use the kithain terms, or the Nunnahi, but I can't seem to find anew equivalent in Spanish or Mayan (or any other native language). Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps Night, Yoatzin, for Unseelie, and Day, <i>tonalli, for Seelie. The other option maybe could be Itzli Seeming, for Obsidian representing Bloody Sacrifice for Unseelie, and Yolcan for Place of Birth for Seelie.</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T03:38:35-07:00","id":1097477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1097453#post1097453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been gettig stuck back in to the Nahuali for the Kingdoms of the Featherd Serpent project, but I've hit a snag. I can't figure out what to call their seemings. It doesn't feel right to use the kithain terms, or the Nunnahi, but I can't seem to find anew equivalent in Spanish or Mayan (or any other native language). Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the seeming? As in childer, wilder and grump?<br /> <br /> How about<b></b>:<br /> Conetl or piltzintli which should both mean a child or perhaps cocone or pipiltoton for children.<br /> <br /> Telpocatl for youth alternativly telpocane for youths.<br /> <br /> Now the Grump is a bit harder... perhaps:<br /> Tlamacatzintli for wise man or tahtli for parent/father or if going for an impression of being older tocoltzitzihuan which should translate to our grandparents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:50:56-07:00","id":1097736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1097465#post1097465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Night, Yoatzin, for Unseelie, and Day, <i>tonalli, for Seelie. The other option maybe could be Itzli Seeming, for Obsidian representing Bloody Sacrifice for Unseelie, and Yolcan for Place of Birth for Seelie.</i><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have the seelie/unseelie already, but thanks (they are Kin (day/sun) and Aak'ab (night)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T03:51:49-07:00","id":1097737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1097477#post1097477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the seeming? As in childer, wilder and grump?<br /> <br /> How about<b></b>:<br /> Conetl or piltzintli which should both mean a child or perhaps cocone or pipiltoton for children.<br /> <br /> Telpocatl for youth alternativly telpocane for youths.<br /> <br /> Now the Grump is a bit harder... perhaps:<br /> Tlamacatzintli for wise man or tahtli for parent/father or if going for an impression of being older tocoltzitzihuan which should translate to our grandparents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gosh, those are great! Where did you get these from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:26:50-07:00","id":1097765,"title":"","content":"First of all I must confess these are from the net so as always take them with a grain of salt as I am unfortunately not a Nahuatl speaker. Still I am relatively confident in these as they can be confirmed through multiple sources. But for a simple site where all of these can be found you might want to check this one out:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://manana.cz/slovnik/nahuaco_en.php\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://manana.cz/slovnik/nahuaco_en.php\" target=\"_blank\"> Please wait... </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://manana.cz/slovnik/nahuaco_en.php\" target=\"_blank\"> http://manana.cz/slovnik/nahuaco_en.php </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T08:27:34-07:00","id":1098439,"title":"","content":"Working on the Baldknobbers as a mix of the original vigilantes and the curse that was laid by the second incarnation that was corrupted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T17:08:15-07:00","id":1098619,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly homebrew, but I would like to nominate the Enchanters from Dreams and Nightmares as a potential Kith. Dreams of wielding magic is prevelant throughout all cultures, so they make an obvious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T17:27:25-07:00","id":1100653,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Nighthawks</b></div> <br /> <br /> There have always been those who lived out of step with society. For some, this has been literal, or rather, chronological: people who walked at night and slept during the day, when others were active. Historically, these were usually people fulfilling a role: guards, servants, parents of newborns. Some few were the odd and unusual, the nightowls and dreamers, star gazers and shamans. In the World of Darkness there would have been more of these, particularly among certain groups such as shifters, mages, and vampires.<br /> <br /> The modern era has seen a marked rise in such people, though. The advent of electricity has allowed more and more people to stay up all night, and lead to all manner of sleeping issues. At present as many as one in eight people work the third shift in some countries, and then there are those who are up all night partying, gaming, reading, binge-watching...<br /> <br /> The Nighthawks arise from their dreams, from those who walk a world others do not get to see, who sleep when other are awake or stagger through life in a drowsy daze. They were once chimera, named by an observant Sluagh for the famous Edward Hopper 1942 painting depicting a handful of people in an all-night cafe in an otherwise abandoned cityscape. They have been called many other things, too: Nightwalkers, Red-Eyes, Dreamweavers, the Sleepless. Like the Wolpertinger, they gained a whole new life during the Resurgence, turning from chimera to a full-fledged Kith. At the time they were still fairly rare, but over time they've grown in number, particuarly in nations and areas where third-shift workers have become far more common. This can be as much the third world as the first world, thanks to the arrival of large factories, mines, and other businesses that operate at night.<br /> <br /> For their part, the Nighthawks find all of the world to be a fascinating place. Their mindset is in ways both alien and familiar, as they often look at things around them with new eyes, in the way that the night time world looks so very different to those new to it, or the way that the daytime world can look strange to those who are. They've become particularly associated with the Chicanery cantrip of Dream Logic, often stating that it feels to them very familiar to their own existence.<br /> <br /> Nighthawks tend to favor being active when others are not; night time, early mornings, weekends, holidays. They are natural contrarians on a certain level. It is not that they are anti-social, but more that they feel a distinctive affinity for these between times; some find them to be comforting, others a thrilling taboo, others marvelous secret to share only those a select few. They likewise are often drawn to places others avoid, whether all of the time or at certain times. One infamous Nighthawk lived in the subway stations in New York City. He would vanish into bathrooms and storage rooms and other niches when they are busy, venturing out between trains, during the off hours, when he would gladly talk to the few who might be about. He had a habit of bestowing small blessings and aid to those he found, particularly regulars such as street musicians or janitors.<br /> <br /> They often take jobs that allow them to wander such places, or similiar work that lets them go to places and times between. Jobs with odd hours and shifts are the most obvious options, but there are others. Some find that traveling lets them do so, as they race between time zones and cities, facing new experiences that those more bound to one location won't understand. Jobs that allow for long distance travel swiftly, such as trucker, train operator, or flying or even working on airlines have often held appeal to them. Interestingly, places like oil rigs, deep sea trawlers, light houses, and weather stations have been known to attract them for similar reasons. Ultimately, they like the between times and places.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: The fae mien of the Nighthawks does not appear to be all there; some say this is because they started out as that moving shadow or strange reflection in the corner of your eye. They're just a little translucent, as is anything they wear or carry for very long, though, thankfully, anything ingested remains hidden. Their skin tends to be an odd hue, just a step off their human form: olive might become gold, dark brown might become dark red. Most notable are their eyes: solidly one color save for pupils, the most frequent hue being, unsurprisingly, red. Dark shades of purple, blue, and green have also been seen, but even among these their eyes turn red when particularly emotional.<br /> <br /> <b>Lifestyles</b>: Nighthawks tend to not like crowds; they are not anti-social, but they prefer to deal with people in smaller numbers, and find a certain beauty to a world less cluttered. Their unique perspectives tend to endear them more to misfits and outsiders, who may not understand them any better but at least appreciate them usually. Others may find them anywhere from quirky to strange to unsettling, depending. As noted, they tend to take jobs that allow them to live on the fringe of society, either physically or chronologically, and sometimes both. They tend not to be afraid of approaching total strangers with their stray observations, though. They often come across as a bit naive and dreamy, and many have been mistaken as drunk or mentally unsound or, in this more modern age, potheads or addicts. The difference between Seelie and Unseelie among Nighthawks is subtle; Seelie are prone to more traditional jobs at odd hours or places, while the Unseelie are more likely to take stranger jobs that let them work more outside the norm, frequently with no set hours. Jobs as artists and writers and photographers might especially appeal, often rooted in childhood or teenage hobbies.<br /> <br /> <b>Childling</b>: These are the kids who stay up late, reading, sneaking out to play with friends or downstairs to watch TV or play video games. They wander the great and mysterious world of Night, which is so very magical and frightening at once to children. Even before they awaken, they are apt to do this.<br /> <br /> <b>Wilder</b>: Wilders are still sneaking out, still cheating on curfews. As they grow older, they start to truly discover the beauty of strange places and times. Some become prone to a particular artform that they may pursue into a career that lets them follow their unusual proclivities: photography, writing, painting. For others, this remains just a hobby, part of their bizarre charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Grump</b>: A grump Nighthawk is a truly strange bird to many. They tend to become more withdrawn or less coherent, and wind up viewed as the neighborhood hermit or oddball. Those prone to solitary jobs often become even more of a loner, while those used to working with others become that weird guy who pops out of nowhere and nobody can understand. Many are so lost in their own skewed view of the world that they hardly understand others. Sadly, quite a few are believed to have dimentia or other mental illnesses and wind up 'treated' for them if not protected by fellow Changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Affinity</b>: Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Revelry</b>: Nighthawks find revelry in discovering beauty in strange places and things. In stalking an empty mall or quiet cafeteria. In wandering a forgotten church or famous tourist destination during the off hours. And, most of all, in sharing their perspective with the few whose paths they might cross, whether they are understood or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Unleashing</b>: Strange shadows or reflections spotted just out of the corner of one's eye lend creedence to the theory that this is how Nighthawks started out. Sounds seem to echo as through an empty hall, and lights to dim. Odors are muted, just the faint remnants of scents many hours old, faded. Sometimes images become fuzzy, as if seen through a heat haze or blurry eyes, and the urge to yawn strikes many.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Birthrights</u></b><br /> <b>Untiring</b> - Nighthawks never get tired. Never. Not only do they not need to sleep, but they never get winded, exhausted, or weary at all. Others sometimes find this unnerving.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Daze</b> - Those who don't get enough sleep often start to hallucinate, moving through a world colored by their half-dreaming mind. Nighthawks have learned to enter this world themselves, but to their benefit. For 1 Glamour, they gain a bonus of -4 diff. to a single simple task. While his could be used to make a normal task ridiculously easy, this is more frequently used to make nearly impossible tasks possible, like picking a lock with a screwdriver. For 2 Glamour this can be a more extensive task, such as driving a getaway car, but the bonus is only -2 difficulty. Either way, for the duration of Dream Daze the Nighthawk becomes very difficult to understand, as they have entered the world of Dream Logic; all social skills suffer +3 difficulty during this time, as are any mental skills not specifically related to the task at hand, as the Nighthawk is effectively both hallucinating and hyperfocusing on that one task. Though this power can be used during combat to perform a task, it can't be used FOR combat; Nighthawks have found that the Dream Daze mindset simply doesn't work for this.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Frailty</u></b><br /> <b>Guileless</b> - Nighthawks have a strange way of looking at the world. They tend to make connections others do not, and miss connections others find commonplace. This causes them problems at times in communicating with others, particularly in matters of subterfuge. It's not that Nighthawks don't understand lies, or what a lie is; it is more that they are prone to missing the cue or taking it the wrong way, and their own efforts are often obscure and disjointed. Nighthawks are at a +3 difficulty for understanding or employing any form of subterfuge; at the ST's discretion this is not necessarily limited to the Subterfuge ability, as efforts by others to be discrete, sarcastic, or clever may also go right over the Nighthawk's head.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Stereotypes</u></b><br /> Dirk Skyggen, Unseelie P.I., opines:<br /> <br /> <b>on Boggans</b> - They're nice to talk to; always listen, very polite, and some of them keep interesting hours like I do. Know one who looks after this concert hall, he never minds if I hang around and chat while he cleans.<br /> <br /> <b>on Clurichauns</b> - Angry little things. Half the time I meet one they say something strange to me and then look confused; by me or their own words I am not certain.<br /> <br /> <b>on Eshu</b> - Fellow wanderers on forgotten paths, they tell us tales and we share with them what we see before they move on. I feel like their ancient relatives of ours.<br /> <br /> <b>on Nockers</b> - They make the most amazing things. They look at machines and things the way we look at the rest of the world, only I don't get nearly so angry when<br /> <br /> <b>on Piskies</b> - I love these guys, so happy and easy-going and, ah, hey, where's my hat?<br /> <br /> <b>on Pooka</b> - Real friendly types, but any time I talk to one after a while they tell me I'm giving them a headache.<br /> <br /> <b>on Redcaps</b> - They're supposed to be so very mean, but I gotta friend works at a all-night cafe says one's his best customer. Must have poor circulation, though, he's always showing up wearing a ski mask.<br /> <br /> <b>on Satyrs</b> - We get along with about half of these guys. Or maybe it's only half the time, I don't know which. One moment they're being all nice and poetic and brooding in a dark corner, and the next they're jogging off to some horrible party.<br /> <br /> <b>on Selkies</b> - I once spent a very lovely evening sitting on a dock with one staring up at the moon. We didn't say a word. When I finally did turn to say something, he was gone. Lovely evening.<br /> <br /> <b>on Arcadian Sidhe</b> - Our paths seldom cross; I have no interest in their courts, and they have no interest in mine.<br /> <br /> <b>on Autumn Sidhe</b> - It might surprise you but I get along with this bunch better than their cousins. They often have an interesting appreciation for our ways.<br /> <br /> <b>on Sluagh</b> - I like these guys. They know the value of secret places, and quiet. My partner, Andy, is one, and he's a great guy. Always telling me to let him do the talking, though. Strange thing for a guy who always whispers to say, huh?<br /> <br /> <b>on Trolls</b> - Big, dark, and quiet. I got a cop friend who's a troll. Straight arrow guy, always looks at me kind of funny, but he never says anything, so I figure we're square.<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: I still might make some adjustments to the Birthrights, I am trying these out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","user":"Windthin","date":". 06-05-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:44:29-07:00","id":1100673,"title":"","content":"Interesting, though the nighthawk birthrites seem kind of strong. I mean never getting tired and -4 diff actions are beefy. It seems more like these guys are active all the time, and are just more active during their chosen time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T22:34:25-07:00","id":1101112,"title":"","content":"So what are thoughts on a Witch Kith and a Warlock Thallain (Thal? What is the Thallain Equivalent to a Kith if they are the equivalent of the name Kithain)? Witches seem like they can be cross Kith, but they would also make a good Kith. With Witches being an Unseelie heavy kith, Warlocks represent those who inspire Legends of the Black Masses and Witches Sabbaths.<br /> <br /> Maybe a frailty preventing harm to innocents, and maybe boons pertaining to sympathetic use of Arts against those you have a link to, or contract with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T22:56:17-07:00","id":1101120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1100653#post1100653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Untiring - Nighthawks never get tired. Never. Not only do they not need to sleep, but they never get winded, exhausted, or weary at all. Others sometimes find this unnerving.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a suggestion... Nighthawks are always feeling a bit tired (you can add that to their Frailty), but never get exhausted or drowsy. <br /> <br /> In fact, you could use a Stamina multiplier to reflect their exceptional endurance while handling particular tasks. While, a Nighthawk pro-gamer with Stamina 1 would be a bit more resilient during a long match without rest or water, Nighthawk clubber with Stamina 5 can literally dance all night, until her shoes are torn to shreds (that's a reference, yeah). Afterwards they promptly return to their normal a-bit-tired state.<br /> <br /> I'd add, though, that they can sleep or rest to restore Willpower and Glamour or heal (while in Freehold), when they want to and the rules apply to them as to everyone else. Just to avoid miscommunication later on.<br /> <br /> I like the kith, overall. Immediately imagined an old Lighthouse watcher. He may be 60 years old. Or 600. He watches the night with his pearcing gaze, guides the ships to their safe harbor and keeps the forces of datkness at bay. <br /> <br /> Actually, Nighthawks may be best buddies with Empire of Flickers. Given, anyone writes this Inanimae Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-07-2017, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:20:40-07:00","id":1101171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1100673#post1100673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, though the nighthawk birthrites seem kind of strong. I mean never getting tired and -4 diff actions are beefy. It seems more like these guys are active all the time, and are just more active during their chosen time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am still tinkering a bit. With the Dream Daze, I was going for something akin to Dream Logic that they can use as an advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths?p=1101120#post1101120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a suggestion... Nighthawks are always feeling a bit tired (you can add that to their Frailty), but never get exhausted or drowsy.<br /> <br /> In fact, you could use a Stamina multiplier to reflect their exceptional endurance while handling particular tasks. While, a Nighthawk pro-gamer with Stamina 1 would be a bit more resilient during a long match without rest or water, Nighthawk clubber with Stamina 5 can literally dance all night, until her shoes are torn to shreds (that's a reference, yeah). Afterwards they promptly return to their normal a-bit-tired state.<br /> <br /> I'd add, though, that they can sleep or rest to restore Willpower and Glamour or heal (while in Freehold), when they want to and the rules apply to them as to everyone else. Just to avoid miscommunication later on.<br /> <br /> I like the kith, overall. Immediately imagined an old Lighthouse watcher. He may be 60 years old. Or 600. He watches the night with his pearcing gaze, guides the ships to their safe harbor and keeps the forces of datkness at bay.<br /> <br /> Actually, Nighthawks may be best buddies with Empire of Flickers. Given, anyone writes this Inanimae Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmm. A Stamina multiplier might not be a bad idea there. I like the idea that they're normally sleepless, drifting through life on a slightly different frequency. I likely can make that work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:47:55-07:00","id":1101184,"title":"","content":"Try this: <b>Untiring</b> - Nighthawks do not require sleep. Instead of sleeping to heal or restore Willpower and Glamour, a Nighthawk will fall into a sort of auto-pilot, quietly tinkering about. They might doodle or write in a journal, sink into a video game, binge watch their favorite series, or just stare out at the sea. They can be rowsed from his state easily enough, but while in it they're effectively disconnected from the world. They also have the ability to stave off exhaustion from heavy activity. Most of the time Nighthawks will seem half-awake, but when they need to they can drawn upon deep reserves. When called upon, a Nighthawk's Stamina is effectively tripled for the purposes of determining how long they can keep functioning without food, water, or rest. Afterwards, they promptly slip back into their normal dazed state. A nighthawk can call upon this ability as many times in a session as they have points of permanent Glamour; at their discretion, an ST may require an expenditure of Willpower or Glamour for particularly large or long undertakings. In the era of energy drinks and coffee places on every corner, these sudden bursts of energy are easily explained away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T03:13:49-07:00","id":1101904,"title":"","content":"I read Dream Daze more closely, and I think it's a bit... complex. At first I expected something more akin to Malkavian madness/wisdom/perception given game mechanics teeth and tangible effect, but from the looks of it, it's more like a Cantrip, rather than Birthright. It has variable costs, variable application, integrated downsides. It's not bad per se, but it's bad game design in general. And on top of that you have second complex-ish Birthright (updated version), which is fine in itself, but together are creating this busy space.<br /> <br /> I would've give it a flat bonus or effect (something like Concetration merit on steroids or making impossible mental leaps), that just works, plus never botching Puzzles Knowledge as an icing on a cake.<br /> <br /> Also, now that I think of it, the idea of Dream Logic sounds a lot like a good alternative for 5th dot of Oneiromancy, for those who find it... limiting. You can temporarily turn a part of Autumn World into the Dreamscape with it's own rules and limitations. And if you think, that it might undermine Firbolg's Birthright, I think that it might benefit from an upgrade itself.<br /> <br /> Also, 5th dot of Oneiromancy previously was just an ability uncorporeal fae (Adhene, Dark-Kin) could use to temporarily affect the Autumn World. Which as a 5th dot won't be all that useful anyway now. As it is, Body Snatching Cantrip is more Nightmare Fuel, than anything else. And some people were riled-up against Satyr's Birthright...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-09-2017, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}